rem            The model asked for "UNSC Marine Armor face". A tags folder holding
rem            "unsc marine armor face.shader_model" does not answer that spelling, so
rem            tool.exe wrote the empty shader under the name it asked for and the head
rem            drew white - with the shader, the bitmap and the texture all correct.
rem            Every material name in the .jms, every tag in "shaders to make.txt" and
rem            the compile script's check are now lower case: a Halo tag path carries
rem            none, and the shader is found by the name the .jms spells. A capitals tag
rem            from an earlier build needs one rename to unsc marine armor face.shader_model
rem            - same folder, same contents, no Guerilla work and no new bitmap.
rem            And the map: a .map carries its own copy of every tag it draws - the
rem            model, its shader references, the bitmap pixels - packed in when it was
rem            built, so a newer model tag changes nothing the game shows. Compile the
rem            model, then build the map again. "Check the shaders.bat" now also says
rem            when a tag is there under the right name and the wrong spelling.
